    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d206">

                <pb facs="0334" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg254"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Conger</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-27"><hi rendition="#italic">September 27,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 569.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 1070, of the 16th ultimo, in regard to the complaints made by certain
                    Chinese residents in Honolulu against the actions of the Chinese consul there
                    and the consequent vicarious punishment of their relatives in China.</p>
                <p>Your note on this subject, addressed to the Chinese Government in compliance with
                    instructions No. 541, of July 2, is approved by the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
